      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coherent interfaces impede dislocation climb.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coherent interfaces reduce atomic diffusion along boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512559::web::012::3_2_steady_state_creep_deformation_behav"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Creep deformation in the relevant regime can be controlled by lattice diffusion of constituent elements.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512559::web::012::3_2_steady_state_creep_deformation_behav"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfaces in HEA-based nanolayered materials can alter dislocation-mediated deformation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9227879::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Impeded climb and reduced diffusion suppress creep-strain accumulation and delay time-dependent plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512559::web::012::3_2_steady_state_creep_deformation_behav"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A coherent-interface multilayer coating will have greater creep resistance than a homogeneous coating.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slight structural or chemical differences between alternating layers can promote coherent, high-strength interfaces.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The multilayer coating will exhibit significantly less time-dependent indentation displacement than the homogeneous baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The multilayer coating will exhibit lower creep strain rates than the homogeneous baseline under identical test conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism is most effective at elevated temperature and moderate stress, where diffusion and dislocation climb are active.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512559::web::012::3_2_steady_state_creep_deformation_behav",
        "PMC11206460::web::028::characterization_of_mobile_dislocations_"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The interface benefit may diminish at low temperatures because dislocation glide dominates.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Extreme service conditions may diminish the benefit by disrupting interface integrity.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The extent of creep suppression depends on layer thickness, interface coherence, and minor compositional variations between layers.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled comparison should use identical substrates and coatings with the same overall composition and total thickness, differing principally in multilayer architecture.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to obtain a statistically significant creep-rate or creep-strain reduction in the multilayer coating would falsify the proposed interface-mediated suppression.",
